 Use it in curries and tea.","breadcrumb":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#breadcrumb"},"inLanguage":"en-US","potentialAction":[{"@type":"ReadAction","target":["https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/"]}]},{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#primaryimage","url":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/turmeric-feature.jpg","contentUrl":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/turmeric-feature.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"caption":"WHITE BOWL full of turmeric powder surrounded by fresh turmeric rhizomes."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#breadcrumb","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Stock Your Pantry with DIY Turmeric Powder for Fresh Flavor"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/#website","url":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/","name":"Attainable Sustainable®","description":"Reviving the lost art of self-reliance, one small step at a time","potentialAction":[{"@type":"SearchAction","target":{"@type":"EntryPoint","urlTemplate":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/?s={search_term_string}"},"query-input":{"@type":"PropertyValueSpecification","valueRequired":true,"valueName":"search_term_string"}}],"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/#\/schema\/person\/1c659a7b0ca5e7fa3bb695adaeb17b71","name":"Kris Bordessa, National Geographic author","description":"Kris Bordessa is an award-winning National Geographic author and a certified Master Food Preserver. Read more about Kris and how she got started with this site here. If you want to send Kris a quick message, you can get in touch here.","sameAs":["attainablesustainable","attainsustain"],"url":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/author\/kris-bordessa\/"},{"@type":"Recipe","name":"Making Turmeric Powder from Fresh Roots","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Kris Bordessa"},"description":"This neon-bright spice has a distinctive flavor that&#x27;s used frequently in Indian cuisine. You can make your own turmeric powder at home from turmeric roots for a fresher product.","datePublished":"2023-01-23T20:03:48+00:00","image":["https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/turmeric-feature.jpg"],"recipeYield":["16","16 servings"],"prepTime":"PT40M","cookTime":"PT300M","totalTime":"PT340M","recipeIngredient":["4 cups turmeric rhizomes"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Thoroughly wash turmeric root. Use a stiff scrub brush to remove most of the outer skin. (It&#x27;s not necessary to peel the turmeric; just remove any really dry or rough patches.)","name":"Thoroughly wash turmeric root. Use a stiff scrub brush to remove most of the outer skin. (It&#x27;s not necessary to peel the turmeric; just remove any really dry or rough patches.)","url":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#wprm-recipe-19144-step-0-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Thinly slice turmeric. Use a food processor equipped with a slicing blade, a mandoline, or simply a knife. Just aim for a uniform thickness, 1\/8&quot; thick or less.","name":"Thinly slice turmeric. Use a food processor equipped with a slicing blade, a mandoline, or simply a knife. Just aim for a uniform thickness, 1\/8&quot; thick or less.","url":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#wprm-recipe-19144-step-0-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Place turmeric root slices on dehydrator trays. ","name":"Place turmeric root slices on dehydrator trays. ","url":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#wprm-recipe-19144-step-0-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Dry at 135 for 5-7 hours, or until the turmeric root is crispy and completely dried. Allow to cool.","name":"Dry at 135 for 5-7 hours, or until the turmeric root is crispy and completely dried. Allow to cool.","url":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#wprm-recipe-19144-step-0-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Place dried turmeric in blender and process until it becomes a fine powder. ","name":"Place dried turmeric in blender and process until it becomes a fine powder. ","url":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#wprm-recipe-19144-step-0-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Store in an airtight container. A glass jar works well, so you can quickly identify it!","name":"Store in an airtight container. A glass jar works well, so you can quickly identify it!","url":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#wprm-recipe-19144-step-0-5"}],"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":"5","ratingCount":"10","reviewCount":"2"},"review":[{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I have been using Turmeric for years but lately it’s not easily available in the stores so I’m going to start growing my own turmeric and other herbs to save money and keep my supplies fresh and well stocked!. \r\nThank you for your very helpful and informative advice on how to achieve my goal!. Sincerely yours \r\nDANimal","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"DANimal Sinneway"},"datePublished":"2025-11-19"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I've been wanting to do this forever but finally have my hands on a borrowed dehydrator! Like many preserving chores, I can't exactly call this a time saver. On the flip side, there is great satisfaction in knowing this is all my work product - from start to finish (except the borrowed dehydrator). I know exactly where my spice came from and how it was processed. I'll always take pride in these accomplishments, knowing I spared carbon by doing it myself (we have solar PV, so as long as I do anything requiring electricity during a sunny day, it's \"free\"). And you can't get any fresher! The flavor is amazing. Thanks Kris!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Susan C"},"datePublished":"2020-01-18"}],"recipeCategory":["Pantry Essentials"],"recipeCuisine":["Indian"],"keywords":"homemade turmeric powder, how to dry olena, how to make turmeric powder, turmeric recipe","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","servingSize":"1 tablespoon","calories":"209 kcal","carbohydrateContent":"38 g","proteinContent":"5 g","sodiumContent":"22 mg","fiberContent":"12 g","fatContent":"6 g","saturatedFatContent":"2 g","sugarContent":"2 g","unsaturatedFatContent":"2 g"},"@id":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#recipe","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/#article"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https:\/\/www.attainable-sustainable.net\/make-turmeric-powder\/"}]}</script>
