<div id="content">
	<div class="container columns">
		<div class="content grt">
			<article id="post-12321" class="post_box text top">
				<div class="headline_area">
					<h1 class="headline">Stock Your Pantry with DIY Turmeric Powder for Fresh Flavor</h1>
					<div class="byline">
						<span class="post_author_intro">Author:</span> <span class="post_author"><a href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/author/kris-bordessa/">Kris Bordessa, National Geographic author</a></span>
						<span class="post_date_intro">Published:</span> <span class="post_date" title="2023-01-23">January 23, 2023</span>
						<span class="post_date_intro">Updated:</span> <span class="post_date date_modified" title="2026-07-21">July 21, 2026</span>
						<a class="num_comments_link" href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/make-turmeric-powder/#comments" rel="nofollow"><span class="num_comments">7</span> comments</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="post_content">
<div class="wprm-recipe wprm-recipe-snippet wprm-recipe-template-as-2024-jump-button"><a href="#recipe" data-recipe="19144" style="color: #000000;background-color: #7ba695;border-color: #7ba695;border-radius: 3px;padding: 5px 8px;" class="wprm-recipe-jump wprm-recipe-link wprm-jump-to-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-normal wprm-recipe-jump-inline-button wprm-recipe-link-inline-button wprm-color-accent"><span class="wprm-recipe-icon wprm-recipe-jump-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><g class="nc-icon-wrapper" fill="#000000"><path data-color="color-2" d="M9,2h6c0.6,0,1-0.4,1-1s-0.4-1-1-1H9C8.4,0,8,0.4,8,1S8.4,2,9,2z"></path> <path fill="#000000" d="M16,11V5c0-0.6-0.4-1-1-1H9C8.4,4,8,4.4,8,5v6H1.9L12,23.6L22.1,11H16z"></path></g></svg></span> Jump to Recipe</a></div><p><strong>Turmeric is easy enough to pick up at the grocery store, certainly, but when one has ready access to freshly grown turmeric it&rsquo;s easy to make turmeric powder at home. Learning how to make turmeric powder ensures the freshest results and good quality turmeric for all of your recipes.</strong></p>
<p><small><em>Originally published November 2018; this post has been updated.</em></small></p>
<img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-30565" src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature.jpg" alt="WHITE BOWL full of turmeric powder surrounded by fresh turmeric rhizomes." width="1200" height="1200" srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature.jpg 1200w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-300x300.jpg 300w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-768x768.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-96x96.jpg 96w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-320x320.jpg 320w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-480x480.jpg 480w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-720x720.jpg 720w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature-735x735.jpg 735w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/turmeric-feature.jpg">
<p>Love the idea of making your own spices? Here&rsquo;s how to make your own <a href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/dried-chile-pepper-flakes/">red pepper flakes</a>!</p>
<p>Fresh turmeric (<em>curcuma longa</em>) roots are similar to ginger &mdash; in fact, it&rsquo;s part of the ginger family &mdash; but the roots are a bit smaller. And much more orange. <strong>Just look at that bright color! </strong>The fresh root will stain surfaces a bright yellow, especially porous surfaces. This is true of turmeric powder, as well.</p>
<h2>Anti-Inflammatory Turmeric</h2>
<p>By now, we&rsquo;ve all heard about turmeric and its <a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8572027/">anti-inflammatory properties</a>, right?</p>
<p>The <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26528921/">National Library of Medicine</a> says this of its medicinal properties:</p><div class="modular">
<div class="deco">
<div class="thrive_suks ml_signup">
<h2 class="h-less"><span style="font-weight: 400;">5 Easy Steps to Transform Your Pantry!</span></h2>
<p>Ready to switch from store bought to homemade? Let me help you make some changes! Grab my FREE five-part guide to getting started.&nbsp;</p>
<p><a class="button save" href="https://attainable-sustainable.myflodesk.com/pantryqsg">Get the Guide!</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<blockquote><p>Turmeric&rsquo;s effects on health are generally centered upon an orange-yellow colored, lipophilic polyphenol substance called &ldquo;curcumin,&rdquo; which is acquired from the rhizomes of the herb. Curcumin is known recently to have antioxidant, anti-inflammatory, anticancer effects and, thanks to these effects, to have an important role in prevention and treatment of various illnesses&hellip;</p></blockquote>
<p><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-12315" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20870%20580'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="fresh turmeric in a white bowl" width="870" height="580" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric.jpg 870w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-150x100.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-350x233.jpg 350w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-550x367.jpg 550w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-380x254.jpg 380w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-260x173.jpg 260w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 870px) 100vw, 870px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric.jpg" data-lazy-src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-12315" src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric.jpg" alt="fresh turmeric in a white bowl" width="870" height="580" srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric.jpg 870w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-150x100.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-350x233.jpg 350w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-550x367.jpg 550w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-380x254.jpg 380w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-260x173.jpg 260w" sizes="(max-width: 870px) 100vw, 870px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric.jpg"></noscript><br>
</p><div class="modular">
<div class="note"><img decoding="async" class="alignleft wp-image-33319 size-medium" style="font-family: system-ui, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, 'Segoe UI', Segoe, 'Helvetica Neue', Tahoma, sans-serif;" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20237%20300'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="cover of Attainable Sustainable Pantry book, featuring numerous pantry items, collage style, on a light green background." width="237" height="300" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1-237x300.jpg 237w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1-118x150.jpg 118w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1-150x190.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1.jpg 600w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 237px) 100vw, 237px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1.jpg" data-lazy-src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1-237x300.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="alignleft wp-image-33319 size-medium" style="font-family: system-ui, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, 'Segoe UI', Segoe, 'Helvetica Neue', Tahoma, sans-serif;" src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1-237x300.jpg" alt="cover of Attainable Sustainable Pantry book, featuring numerous pantry items, collage style, on a light green background." width="237" height="300" srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1-237x300.jpg 237w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1-118x150.jpg 118w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1-150x190.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 237px) 100vw, 237px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/attainable-pantry-cover-for-site-1.jpg"></noscript><span style="font-family: system-ui, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, 'Segoe UI', Segoe, 'Helvetica Neue', Tahoma, sans-serif;">Ready to DIY your pantry with more wholesome ingredients? Check out my new book from National Geographic! </span><a style="font-family: system-ui, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, 'Segoe UI', Segoe, 'Helvetica Neue', Tahoma, sans-serif;" href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/attainable-sustainable-pantry/"><em>Attainable Sustainable Pantry</em></a><span style="font-family: system-ui, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, 'Segoe UI', Segoe, 'Helvetica Neue', Tahoma, sans-serif;"> is filled with delicious recipes for some of your favorite condiments, snacks, and toppings, along with an entire section on <strong><em>safe</em></strong> home food preservation. It&rsquo;s the guide you need to start </span><strong style="font-family: system-ui, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, 'Segoe UI', Segoe, 'Helvetica Neue', Tahoma, sans-serif;">skipping packaged products</strong><span style="font-family: system-ui, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, 'Segoe UI', Segoe, 'Helvetica Neue', Tahoma, sans-serif;"> and embrace homemade.</span></div>
</div>

<h3>Ingredients for Fresh Turmeric Powder</h3>
<p>Your best bet for finding turmeric root is at an ethnic food store, though you <a href="https://www.facebook.com/hip.agriculture/posts/911249678987826?" target="_blank" rel="noopener">may be able to order it online</a> as well. Once you&rsquo;ve acquired fresh turmeric rhizomes, be sure to set a few aside so you can start growing your own!</p>
<p>This plant typically grows in tropical regions, but gardeners in less temperate regions can grow it in a pot, which allows you to protect the plant from cold weather and extend the growing season. <a href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/turmeric/">Learn how to grow a turmeric plant</a>.</p>
<h3>How to Dry Turmeric Root</h3>
<p>Spoiler: <em>It&rsquo;s easy.&nbsp;</em></p>
<p>To make turmeric powder, you&rsquo;ll need to remove all of the moisture from the turmeric fingers. (And indeed, they do look like fingers!)</p>
<p>This is achieved by slicing the turmeric thinly, and then dehydrating it. I use a dehydrator, but this can certainly be done in an oven set to low as well.</p>
<p>There&rsquo;s no need to peel the raw turmeric root if it&rsquo;s fresh. A stiff scrub brush will remove residual dirt as well as some of the soft skins. If you do want to remove the skin, the easiest way to do so is by scraping the root with the side of a spoon.</p>
<img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-12314" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20870%20580'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="fresh turmeric, sliced in a food processor bowl" width="870" height="580" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1.jpg 870w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-150x100.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-350x233.jpg 350w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-550x367.jpg 550w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-380x254.jpg 380w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-260x173.jpg 260w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 870px) 100vw, 870px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1.jpg" data-lazy-src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-12314" src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1.jpg" alt="fresh turmeric, sliced in a food processor bowl" width="870" height="580" srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1.jpg 870w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-150x100.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-350x233.jpg 350w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-550x367.jpg 550w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-380x254.jpg 380w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1-260x173.jpg 260w" sizes="(max-width: 870px) 100vw, 870px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-1.jpg"></noscript>
<p>Once clean, slice fresh turmeric root into uniform thickness. I used my food processor, but a mandoline would work, as would a knife. The thinner the slices, the faster they&rsquo;ll dry in the dehydrator.</p>
<h3>Using a Dehydrator</h3>
<p>A food dehydrator is a specialized appliance specifically made for drying fruits, veggies, and meat. They come in a variety of shapes and sizes, but all include a number of trays that allow warm air to freely circulate.</p>
<p>This is my preferred method of drying produce. My 9-tray Excalibur dehydrator holds the largest amount of produce out of all three of the methods listed here, <strong>making the most of the energy used</strong>&nbsp;to dry them.</p>
<p data-slot-rendered-content="true">Place turmeric slices in a single layer, fitting as many as you can without overlapping, on the dehydrator trays and dry at 135&ordm;F for 5-7 hours.</p>
<div id="attachment_12319" style="width: 880px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-12319" class="wp-image-12319 size-full" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20870%20580'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="sliced fresh turmeric on dehydrator tray" width="870" height="580" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder.jpg 870w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-150x100.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-350x233.jpg 350w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-550x367.jpg 550w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-380x254.jpg 380w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-260x173.jpg 260w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 870px) 100vw, 870px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder.jpg" data-lazy-src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-12319" class="wp-image-12319 size-full" src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder.jpg" alt="sliced fresh turmeric on dehydrator tray" width="870" height="580" srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder.jpg 870w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-150x100.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-350x233.jpg 350w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-550x367.jpg 550w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-380x254.jpg 380w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-260x173.jpg 260w" sizes="(max-width: 870px) 100vw, 870px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder.jpg"></noscript><p id="caption-attachment-12319" class="wp-caption-text">Fill the trays of a dehydrator without allowing too much of the root to overlap.</p></div>
<h3>Oven Drying</h3>
<p data-slot-rendered-dynamic="true">Drying turmeric in the oven utilizes equipment most people already have on hand. It&rsquo;s not the most <strong>energy-efficient</strong>&nbsp;method, but it does the trick in a pinch.</p>
<p>Set the oven to a low temperature. 135&ordm;F is the ideal, but not all ovens offer that precise low heat. If you have an oven with a bread proofing setting you can try that. Older ovens that only go as low as 200&ordm;F can be used, but you&rsquo;ll need to prop the oven door open.</p>
<p>Place sliced turmeric on a wire rack on a baking sheet. This allows the air to flow around the slices. Alternatively, you can line each baking tray with parchment paper.</p>
<p>The amount of time required for oven drying will vary depending on the temperature you are able to use.</p>
<h3>Sun Drying</h3>
<p>In warm, dry regions, you can try your hand at sun-dried turmeric. Prepare the turmeric as for oven drying and place the trays outside out of direct sunlight. Cover with a light tea towel or a layer of cheesecloth to prevent insects from landing on the food.</p>
<div id="attachment_12317" style="width: 880px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-12317" class="wp-image-12317 size-full" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20870%20580'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="dried turmeric on a dehydrator tray" width="870" height="580" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1.jpg 870w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-150x100.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-350x233.jpg 350w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-550x367.jpg 550w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-380x254.jpg 380w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-260x173.jpg 260w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 870px) 100vw, 870px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1.jpg" data-lazy-src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-12317" class="wp-image-12317 size-full" src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1.jpg" alt="dried turmeric on a dehydrator tray" width="870" height="580" srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1.jpg 870w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-150x100.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-350x233.jpg 350w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-550x367.jpg 550w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-380x254.jpg 380w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1-260x173.jpg 260w" sizes="(max-width: 870px) 100vw, 870px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-1.jpg"></noscript><p id="caption-attachment-12317" class="wp-caption-text">The turmeric root loses its bright yellow color once dried.</p></div>
<h3>Checking for Doneness</h3>
<p>Be sure to dry it until it&rsquo;s crispy and cracks easily in two when you bend it. This assures that the moisture content is low enough for long-term storage.</p>
<h3>Processing the Dried Turmeric Root</h3>
<p>When you&rsquo;ve achieved the right level of dryness, transfer the dried turmeric to a blender or spice grinder and process until it&rsquo;s a fine powder. You may want to sift out the finest powder and reprocess the larger bits.</p>
<p>You can also pulse to create small pieces of turmeric that are just shy of a powder. These make a good addition to tea blends.</p>
<img decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-27802" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="spoonful of orange turmeric powder, with a small jar full behind." width="1200" height="1200" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4.jpg 1200w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-300x300.jpg 300w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-768x768.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-96x96.jpg 96w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-320x320.jpg 320w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-480x480.jpg 480w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-720x720.jpg 720w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-735x735.jpg 735w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4.jpg" data-lazy-src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4.jpg"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-27802" src="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4.jpg" alt="spoonful of orange turmeric powder, with a small jar full behind." width="1200" height="1200" srcset="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4.jpg 1200w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-300x300.jpg 300w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-768x768.jpg 768w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-96x96.jpg 96w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-320x320.jpg 320w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-480x480.jpg 480w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-720x720.jpg 720w, https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4-735x735.jpg 735w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/turmeric-powder-4.jpg"></noscript>
<h3>Storage</h3>
<p>Store the dried root, powder, or pieces in an airtight container in a dry place. If you live in a humid region, as I do, these <a href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/desiccant/">homemade desiccant packs</a> can extend the shelf life of your homemade turmeric powder.</p>
<h3>FAQs</h3>
<p><strong>Do I need to peel turmeric before consuming?</strong></p>
<p>The peel is completely edible. You can scrub it or peel it, or do nothing beyond washing the turmeric root. I&rsquo;m all for saving time in the kitchen, so I scrub well so any dirty or loose peel comes off but I don&rsquo;t necessarily peel every last bit off.</p>
<p><strong>How long can I store turmeric powder?</strong></p>
<p>Purchasing or making desiccant packs is ideal for storage. You can also vacuum seal or use self-sealing mylar bags as well. Only leave out enough that you can use in a reasonable amount of time so the remainder stays fresh. I&rsquo;d say the best potency is about a year, especially if you store it carefully.</p>
<p><strong>Does turmeric stain?</strong></p>
<p>You can wear gloves when processing turmeric, as it will stain much like when working with beets. Protect your work surface with an old towel or a baking sheet. Keep in mind that your food processor or other equipment may also be stained by this!</p>
<p><strong>Do I need to use a dehydrator?</strong></p>
<p>Drying the turmeric in a dehydrator uses a lower, gentler heat than using the oven, though it does take longer. You can use the oven if you don&rsquo;t have a dehydrator or have less time. It is still a low enough heat to not destroy the health benefits of turmeric. Some people even dry their turmeric root in the sun, but it can take as long as two weeks! And if you live where it&rsquo;s humid as I do, I don&rsquo;t think it would ever dry out completely.</p>
<h3>Using Turmeric Powder</h3>
<ul>
<li>Add it to this easy <a href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/curry-powder-recipe/">curry powder</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/chicken-noodle-soup-recipe/">Jazz up chicken noodle soup</a></li>
<li><a style="cursor: pointer !important; user-select: none !important;" href="https://rootsy.org/golden-milk-recipe/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Make golden milk</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/green-onion-dip-recipe/">Stir some into this homemade green onion dip</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/dye-easter-eggs-naturally/" rel="noopener">Use it as a dye</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.attainable-sustainable.net/gourmet-mustard/">Add it to your homemade mustard recipe</a></li>
